\section*{Question 6}

Let \(f\) be the function satisfying \(f^{\prime}(x)=x \sqrt{f(x)}\) for all real numbers \(x\), where \(f(3)=25\).
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Find \(f^{\prime \prime}(3)\).
\item[(b)] Write an expression for \(y=f(x)\) by solving the differential equation \(\frac{d y}{d x}=x \sqrt{y}\) with the initial condition \(f(3)=25\).
\item[(a)] \(f^{\prime \prime}(x)=\sqrt{f(x)}+x \cdot \frac{f^{\prime}(x)}{2 \sqrt{f(x)}}=\sqrt{f(x)}+\frac{x^{2}}{2}\)
\[
f^{\prime \prime}(3)=\sqrt{25}+\frac{9}{2}=\frac{19}{2}
\]
\item[(b)] \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{y}} d y=x d x\)
\[
\begin{aligned}
& 2 \sqrt{y}=\frac{1}{2} x^{2}+C \\
& 2 \sqrt{25}=\frac{1}{2}(3)^{2}+C ; C=\frac{11}{2} \\
& \sqrt{y}=\frac{1}{4} x^{2}+\frac{11}{4} \\
& y=\left(\frac{1}{4} x^{2}+\frac{11}{4}\right)^{2}=\frac{1}{16}\left(x^{2}+11\right)^{2}
\end{aligned}
\]
\end{itemize}
\(3:\left\{\begin{aligned} 2: & f^{\prime \prime}(x) \\ & <-2>\text { product or } \\ & \text { chain rule error } \\ 1: & \text { value at } x=3\end{aligned}\right.\)
